= Machine consciousness (simple) =

'''Machine consciousness''' asks whether a computer or AI system could actually have experiences, rather than merely process information or say that it has experiences.

Today's AI systems can learn patterns, reason about tasks, communicate and sometimes keep records about themselves. Scientists do not agree on a test that would prove those abilities come with subjective experience.

Researchers compare possible signs of consciousness using theories about the brain and information processing. None is a universally accepted yes-or-no test.

